{"description":"M5 — make the strategy falsifiable. The Layer-2 capture already stores sessionId, sourcePromptHash and provenance; add the derived signals that say whether the mechanisms are being used: did a session read a binding before writing, did it fail a gate, did it repair the violation in the same session? Aggregate per repository and per period into a small report with cost and step counts. Without these numbers M2 versus M3a cannot be compared honestly, and the recent lesson in this repository is that a claim without a number is how a defect sits unnoticed.","acceptanceCriteria":"- A command reports, per repository and period: sessions observed, sessions that retrieved a constraint before their first write, gate failures, and violations repaired within the same session.\n- All four numbers are derived from captured provenance and session identifiers already stored; no new capture fields are invented for this item.\n- The report is deterministic for a fixed store state and supports --json.\n- A test builds a fixture store with one compliant and one non-compliant session and asserts both aggregates.\n- The report states its own limits (sessions without capture, sessions that predate the signal) rather than presenting a bare number."}